; An untyped constant expression into a narrow parameter is a constant of the
; parameter's width (2026-10-19, Planner.settle_constant#): `take32(0 - 1)`
; passes `i32 -1`. Before it passed `i64 -1` into the i32 parameter -- the
; callee type is built from the arguments, so nothing objected, and a callee
; that reads the whole register saw 2^32 - 1 (the http package's
; scaly_eio_stat call did exactly this).
; expect-ir: call i64 @_Z6take323i32(i32 -1)
function take32(n: i32) returns int
    n as int

print "`take32(0 - 1)`"
